T1520	Entity 149754 149761	Scrooge
T1521	Quotation 149763 149810	"It's a pleasure to talk to him. Yes, my buck!"
T1522	Quotation 149812 149837	"It's hanging there now,"
T1523	Cue 149838 149845	replied
T1524	Quotation 149856 149864	"Is it?"
T1525	Cue 149865 149869	said
T1526	Entity 149870 149877	Scrooge
T1527	Quotation 149879 149895	"Go and buy it."
T1528	Quotation 149897 149907	"Walk-er!"
T1529	Cue 149908 149917	exclaimed
T1530	Quotation 149928 149937	"No, no,"
T1531	Cue 149938 149942	said
T1532	Entity 149943 149950	Scrooge
T1533	Quotation 149952 150201	"I am in earnest. Go and buy it, and tell 'em to bring it here, that I may give them the direction where to take it. Come back with the man, and I'll give you a shilling. Come back with him in less than five minutes, and I'll give you half-a-crown!"
T1534	Quotation 150321 150354	"I'll send it to Bob Cratchit's!"
T1535	Cue 150355 150364	whispered
T1536	Entity 150365 150372	Scrooge
T1537	Quotation 150421 150551	"He sha'n't know who sends it. It's twice the size of Tiny Tim. Joe Miller never made such a joke as sending it to Bob's will be!"
T1538	Quotation 150804 150841	"I shall love it, as long as I live!"
T1539	Cue 150842 150847	cried
T1540	Entity 150848 150855	Scrooge
T1541	Quotation 150883 151056	"I scarcely ever looked at it before. What an honest expression it has in its face! It's a wonderful knocker!—Here's the Turkey. Hallo! Whoop! How are you! Merry Christmas!"
T1542	Quotation 151205 151257	"Why, it's impossible to carry that to Camden Town,"
T1543	Cue 151258 151262	said
T1544	Entity 151263 151270	Scrooge
T1545	Quotation 151272 151294	"You must have a cab."
T1546	Entity 152203 152238	three or four good-humoured fellows
T1547	Cue 152239 152243	said
T1548	Quotation 152245 152291	"Good morning, sir! A merry Christmas to you!"
T1549	Entity 152296 152303	Scrooge
T1550	Entity 152471 152491	the portly gentleman
T1551	Cue 152551 152555	said
T1552	Quotation 152557 152591	"Scrooge and Marley's, I believe?"
T1553	Quotation 152755 152769	"My dear sir,"
T1554	Cue 152770 152774	said
T1555	Entity 152775 152782	Scrooge
T1556	Quotation 152853 152957	"How do you do? I hope you succeeded yesterday. It was very kind of you. A merry Christmas to you, sir!"
T1557	Quotation 152959 152973	"Mr. Scrooge?"
T1558	Quotation 152975 152981	"Yes,"
T1559	Cue 152982 152986	said
T1560	Entity 152987 152994	Scrooge
T1561	Quotation 152996 153116	"That is my name, and I fear it may not be pleasant to you. Allow me to ask your pardon. And will you have the goodness"
T1562	Cue 153130 153150	whispered in his ear
T1563	Quotation 153153 153169	"Lord bless me!"
T1564	Cue 153170 153175	cried
T1565	Entity 153176 153189	the gentleman
T1566	Quotation 153219 153258	"My dear Mr. Scrooge, are you serious?"
T1567	Quotation 153260 153276	"If you please,"
T1568	Cue 153277 153281	said
T1569	Entity 153282 153289	Scrooge
T1570	Quotation 153291 153402	"Not a farthing less. A great many back-payments are included in it, I assure you. Will you do me that favour?"
T1571	Quotation 153404 153418	"My dear sir,"
T1572	Cue 153419 153423	said
T1573	Quotation 153459 153501	"I don't know what to say to such munifi—"
T1574	Quotation 153503 153532	"Don't say anything, please,"
T1575	Cue 153533 153541	retorted
T1576	Entity 153542 153549	Scrooge
T1577	Quotation 153551 153595	"Come and see me. Will you come and see me?"
T1578	Quotation 153597 153606	"I will!"
T1579	Cue 153607 153612	cried
T1580	Entity 153613 153630	the old gentleman
T1581	Quotation 153669 153680	"Thank'ee,"
T1582	Cue 153681 153685	said
T1583	Entity 153686 153693	Scrooge
T1584	Quotation 153695 153758	"I am much obliged to you. I thank you fifty times. Bless you!"
T1585	Quotation 154293 154327	"Is your master at home, my dear?"
T1586	Cue 154328 154332	said
T1587	Entity 154333 154340	Scrooge
T1588	Entity 154344 154352	the girl
T1589	Quotation 154372 154383	"Yes, sir."
T1590	Quotation 154385 154408	"Where is he, my love?"
T1591	Cue 154409 154413	said
T1592	Entity 154414 154421	Scrooge
T1593	Quotation 154424 154516	"He's in the dining-room, sir, along with mistress. I'll show you up stairs, if you please."
T1594	Quotation 154518 154542	"Thank'ee. He knows me,"
T1595	Cue 154543 154547	said
T1596	Entity 154548 154555	Scrooge
T1597	Quotation 154604 154631	"I'll go in here, my dear."
T1598	Quotation 154871 154878	"Fred!"
T1599	Cue 154879 154883	said
T1600	Entity 154884 154891	Scrooge
T1601	Quotation 155084 155104	"Why bless my soul!"
T1602	Cue 155105 155110	cried
T1603	Entity 155111 155115	Fred
T1604	Quotation 155117 155130	"who's that?"
T1605	Quotation 155132 155210	"It's I. Your uncle Scrooge. I have come to dinner. Will you let me in, Fred?"
T1606	Quotation 156112 156120	"Hallo!"
T1607	Cue 156121 156128	growled
T1608	Entity 156129 156136	Scrooge
T1609	Quotation 156192 156246	"What do you mean by coming here at this time of day?"
T1610	Quotation 156248 156270	"I'm very sorry, sir,"
T1611	Cue 156271 156275	said
T1612	Entity 156276 156279	Bob
T1613	Quotation 156281 156303	"I am behind my time."
T1614	Quotation 156305 156315	"You are?"
T1615	Cue 156316 156324	repeated
T1616	Entity 156325 156332	Scrooge
T1617	Quotation 156334 156387	"Yes. I think you are. Step this way, if you please."
T1618	Quotation 156389 156418	"It's only once a year, sir,"
T1619	Cue 156419 156426	pleaded
T1620	Entity 156427 156430	Bob
T1621	Quotation 156457 156526	"It shall not be repeated. I was making rather merry yesterday, sir."
T1622	Quotation 156528 156565	"Now, I'll tell you what, my friend,"
T1623	Cue 156566 156570	said
T1624	Entity 156571 156578	Scrooge
T1625	Quotation 156580 156651	"I am not going to stand this sort of thing any longer. And therefore,"
T1626	Quotation 156777 156825	"and therefore I am about to raise your salary!"
T1627	Quotation 157023 157048	"A merry Christmas, Bob!"
T1628	Cue 157049 157053	said
T1629	Entity 157054 157061	Scrooge
T1630	Quotation 157142 157486	"A merrier Christmas, Bob, my good fellow, than I have given you, for many a year! I'll raise your salary, and endeavour to assist your struggling family, and we will discuss your affairs this very afternoon, over a Christmas bowl of smoking bishop, Bob!  Make up the fires, and buy another coal-scuttle before you dot another i, Bob Cratchit!"
